    "04/17/2026",
    "According to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDCExternal Link), social isolation can negatively affect youth physical health, mental health, and academic performance. Disconnected students face increased risks of:",
    "Academic failure and truancy",
    "Academic failure and truancy",
    "Anxiety and depression",
    "Anxiety and depression",
    "Sleep disorders",
    "Sleep disorders",
    "Cardiovascular disease",
    "Cardiovascular disease",
    "Self‑harm",
    "Self‑harm",
    "Creating welcoming school environments that promote connection and belonging is an important part of supporting student well‑being. To help address these challenges, the Centene Foundation supports community‑based efforts that strengthen peer connection and a sense of belonging in schools.",
    "Since 2017, the Centene Foundation has supported No One Eats Alone®External Link, a national program led by Sandy Hook PromiseExternal Link. This program helps schools:",
    "Encourage peer connection",
    "Encourage peer connection",
    "Build welcoming school environments",
    "Build welcoming school environments",
    "Support students who may feel left out",
    "Support students who may feel left out",
    "Schools also receive the No One Eats Alone curriculum and materials in a Belonging Box at no cost, supporting local efforts to create more welcoming and connected school communities.",
    "In 2026, Centene’s partnership resulted in more than 5,000 school registrations and over three million students participating nationwide. Several of Centene’s health plans have been running local events for close to a decade. This year, participating plans included WellCare of KentuckyExternal Link, Superior HealthPlanExternal Link, and Coordinated CareExternal Link.",
    "The Centene Foundation continues to support education through programs like No One Eats Alone Day, helping students across the country learn valuable skills to connect with their classmates and provide a sense of belonging.",
    "A Belonging Box for schools, filled with materials and activities, is sponsored by the Centene Foundation.",
    "View Partnerships >",
    "Transforming the health of the communities we serve, one person at a time.",
    "HEALTHCARE IS BEST DELIVERED LOCALLY",
    "Our uniquely local approach allows us to help members access quality-focused, culturally sensitive healthcare services.",
    "CENTENE IS COMMITTED TO CORPORATE SUSTAINABILITY",
    "The health of individuals drives our focus on the environment, removing social barriers to health and prioritizing responsible corporate governance.",
    "© Copyright 2026 Centene Corporation"
